# Rust Workflow

- Use the latest stable Rust toolchain unless a crate or target requires otherwise.
- Prefer `cargo add` for new dependencies so versions come from the registry instead of guesses.
- Write tests before implementation for crypto-lab primitives and security-sensitive core behavior.
- Run `cargo fmt --all` and `cargo test --workspace` after substantive Rust changes.
- For production code, add `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets` once the clippy component is installed.
- Keep `/core` independent from `/crypto-lab`; tests may compare behavior, but production code must not depend on educational implementations.

